{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' docs/PRD.md\"","aggregated_output":"/opt/homebrew/Library/Homebrew/cmd/shellenv.sh: line 18: /bin/ps: Operation not permitted\n# HeroKid - Product Requirements Document\n\n**Author:** Doğan\n**Date:** 2025-11-11\n**Version:** 1.0\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nHeroKid is an AI-powered personalized storytelling platform that transforms children aged 5-12 into the heroes of their own adventures alongside their real pets as magical companions. Unlike generic story generators that swap names into templates, HeroKid creates authentic emotional connections by featuring the child's actual visual appearance across multiple professional art styles, their beloved pets as story companions, and creates a persistent library of personalized adventures.\n\nThe platform addresses a critical market gap: existing children's storytelling apps offer either static libraries without personalization (Epic) or AI generation with shallow customization (Bedtimestory.ai). HeroKid combines the professional quality and consistency of curated content with the emotional depth of true personalization - it's REALLY the child, their REAL pet, in THEIR unique story.\n\n**MVP Strategy:** Launch simultaneously on iOS and Android with web-based parental dashboard, focusing on visual personalization and story quality. Voice narration and advanced AI features planned for post-MVP phases to accelerate time-to-market.\n\n### What Makes This Special\n\n**The Emotional Trinity:** HeroKid creates unprecedented psychological investment through three breakthrough innovations:\n\n1. **Authentic Visual Personalization** - Children see themselves as consistent, professional-quality cartoon characters across 4 art styles (Pixar 3D, 2D Cartoon, Anime, Watercolor), not generic avatars\n2. **Real Pet Integration** - Beloved family pets transform into magical story companions, creating emotional anchors that drive engagement\n3. **Professional Quality + Child Agency** - Disney-level visual consistency combined with meaningful choices (art style, adventure type, companion inclusion)\n\nThe magic formula: **Maximum emotional connection (it's ME and MY PET) + professional quality + child agency = unprecedented engagement and family loyalty.**\n\n---\n\n## Project Classification\n\n**Technical Type:** Mobile App (iOS/Android) + Web App (Parental Dashboard)\n**Domain:** Educational Technology (EdTech)\n**Complexity:** Medium-High\n\n**Platform Architecture:**\n- React Native cross-platform mobile apps for iOS 14+ and Android 8+ powered by Expo + EAS\n- Next.js 15 web dashboard for parental controls and credit management hosted on Vercel\n- Backend: Supabase (PostgreSQL, Auth, Storage) for relational data, authentication, and media storage\n- API: tRPC on Next.js 15 API routes for fully typed communication between web and mobile clients\n- Hosting: Vercel (web/API) with EAS (mobile) for build, distribution, and OTA updates\n- Monorepo: Turborepo with `apps/mobile`, `apps/web`, and `packages/shared`\n- Deployment: Vercel serverless functions orchestrated via GitHub Actions CI/CD\n- AI Services: Google Gemini (text) and Nano Banana image APIs remain on GCP but are consumed via managed secrets\n\n**Domain Complexity Drivers:**\n- Child privacy regulations (COPPA, GDPR-K compliance mandatory)\n- Age-appropriate content moderation and safety filtering\n- Educational value and developmental appropriateness across age groups (5-7, 8-10, 11-12)\n- Sensitive data handling (photos must be deleted within 24-48 hours)\n- Parental controls and family safety features\n\n### Domain Context\n\n**EdTech Regulatory Environment:**\n\nHeroKid operates in a highly regulated space requiring careful navigation of child privacy laws, content safety standards, and educational technology best practices.\n\n**Critical Compliance Requirements:**\n- **COPPA (Children's Online Privacy Protection Act):** Parental consent for data collection, verifiable parental consent mechanisms, strict data minimization, photo deletion audit trails\n- **GDPR-K (GDPR provisions for children):** Enhanced protections for children under 13, right to deletion, data portability, transparent privacy notices in child-friendly language\n- **Content Safety:** Multi-layered content moderation combining AI filtering with human review, age-appropriate content standards, family-friendly themes exclusively\n\n**Privacy-First Architecture:**\n- Photo uploads deleted within 24-48 hours after avatar generation\n- Generated avatars stored permanently (not source photos)\n- End-to-end encryption for user data\n- SOC 2 certification requirements for enterprise trust\n- Clear audit trails for compliance demonstration\n\n**Developmental Appropriateness:**\nThe platform must adapt content complexity, themes, and interaction patterns across three distinct developmental stages:\n- Ages 5-7: Simple linear narratives, clear heroes/villains, magical elements\n- Ages 8-10: Longer episodic adventures, skill mastery themes, team dynamics\n- Ages 11-12: Complex narratives with moral depth, identity exploration, epic challenges\n\n---\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n**Success means children experience the \"that's ME!\" moment of recognition and parents feel confident in both safety and educational value.**\n\n### User Success Metrics (Primary Indicators)\n\n**Engagement & Emotional Connection:**\n- **85%+ story completion rate** - Children finish stories they start, indicating emotional investment\n- **Children request new stories 3+ times per week** - Organic return usage demonstrating genuine desire\n- **90% of children choose to include pets when available** - Validation of pet companion emotional anchor\n- **Users try all 4 art styles within first month** - Exploration behavior indicating creative engagement\n\n**Family Integration:**\n- **Parents feel confident about privacy/safety after onboarding** - Trust established through transparent controls\n- **70%+ monthly repurchase for active credit buyers** - Families continue topping up credits because they see value\n\n**Technical Quality:**\n- **95%+ avatar recognition across scenes** - Visual consistency maintains immersion and suspension of disbelief\n- **All three age segments (5-7, 8-10, 11-12) engage with age-appropriate complexity** - Content successfully adapts\n\n### Business Metrics\n\n**Revenue & Growth:**\n- **$2M+ ARR by Year 2** through credit-based model (flexible per-use spending)\n- **100K registered users by Month 12** with **40K+ credit purchasers** (40% conversion rate - lower friction than subscriptions)\n- **Average $8-15/month spending per engaged family** - Flexible spending based on usage not fixed tier\n\n**Market Position:**\n- **Net Promoter Score (NPS) of 70+** - Industry-leading satisfaction and word-of-mouth growth\n- **Establish as premium leader** in personalized children's content (not competing on price)\n\n**Operational Efficiency:**\n- **Support 1000+ concurrent users** without performance degradation in MVP\n- **<$500K development cost** to MVP launch with seed funding runway\n\n### Definition of MVP Success\n\nMVP is successful if these gates are passed:\n1. ✅ Children complete 80%+ of started stories and request new ones within 48 hours\n2. ✅ Parents complete full onboarding and feel confident about privacy/safety\n3. ✅ Avatar consistency maintains immersion (95%+ recognition)\n4. ✅ Core adventure templates engage all three age segments appropriately\n5. ✅ Platform supports 1000+ concurrent users with <30 second story generation\n\n---\n\n## Product Scope\n\n### MVP - Minimum Viable Product\n\n**Core Value Proposition:** Authentic visual personalization + beloved pet companions + professional-quality storytelling in mobile apps for iOS and Android, delivered through a **flexible credit-based monetization model**.\n\n**Monetization Model (Credit-Based - November 2025 Pivot):**\n\nBased on user feedback and operational simplicity, HeroKid transitioned from subscription tiers to a credit-based system that provides flexibility for families while ensuring sustainable unit economics:\n\n**Free Offerings (Per Family Account):**\n- **First Child Only:** 1 free avatar creation (2 images: headshot + full body) + 1 free pet companion\n- **All Children:** 20 generic free stories always available in library\n- **Unlimited Re-reads:** Previous stories can be read unlimited times (no credits)\n\n**Credit-Based Pricing (Per Action):**\n- **Avatar Creation:** 4 credits\n  - First child: FREE\n  - Additional children: 4 credits each\n  - Can create multiple avatars in different styles (4 credits per additional avatar)\n- **Pet Companion Creation:** 4 credits\n  - First child: FREE\n  - Additional children: 4 credits each\n- **Story Generation (Customized):** 10 credits\n  - Applies to all children (including first child after free avatar created)\n  - Only for customized stories (child's avatar + pet)\n  - Generic stories always free\n\n**Credit Packages (Purchase):**\n- **20 credits:** $1.99\n- **50 credits:** $3.99 (Popular - Best value)\n- **100 credits:** $6.99 (Best savings)\n- **Credits never expire** - No time pressure on spending\n\n**Credit Pricing Examples:**\n- 1 avatar = 4 credits (~$0.40-$0.16 depending on package bought)\n- 1 story = 10 credits (~$1.00-$0.42 depending on package bought)\n- 5 stories + 2 avatars = 60 credits (~$6.00-$2.40 depending on package)\n\n**Why Credit Model:**\n- ✅ **Flexibility:** Families pay only for what they use (no monthly commitment)\n- ✅ **COPPA-compliant:** No subscriptions = simpler regulatory compliance\n- ✅ **No waste:** Parents never overpay for unused monthly allowances\n- ✅ **Pay-as-you-go:** Organic spending based on actual usage patterns\n- ✅ **Aligns incentives:** We want kids engaged (more stories) not capped by tier\n- ✅ **Easier payment:** One-time purchase vs. recurring subscription friction\n\n**Expected Performance (Credit Model):**\n- Average family spends $5-15/month when engaged (1-3 stories + 1 avatar)\n- No subscription churn concerns (pay per use)\n- Higher lifetime value for engaged families (no spending cap)\n- Easier trial-to-paid conversion (small credit pack purchase vs. subscription commitment)\n\n---\n\n### Core Features (MVP)\n\n**1. Multi-Avatar Creation System**\n   - Upload portal: Portrait photo + full-body photo via mobile camera or gallery (2 images required)\n   - AI processing: Generate 4 art style avatars (Pixar 3D, 2D Cartoon, Anime, Watercolor) using Nano Banana API\n   - Storage: Generated avatars stored permanently in user profile; source photos deleted from server 24-48 hours after generation\n   - Device storage: Photos also stored on user's device for future use (no re-upload needed)\n   - Privacy compliance: Source photos deleted from server within 24-48 hours with audit trail\n   - Avatar preview: Side-by-side comparison of all 4 styles before story generation\n   - **Cost**: First child: FREE | Additional children: 4 credits each (~$0.16-$0.40 depending on credit package)\n\n**2. Pet Companion Integration**\n   - Pet photo upload with same privacy protocol (delete from server 24-48 hours after processing)\n   - Device storage: Pet photos stored on user's device for future use\n   - Transform pet into story-appropriate magical companion matching selected art style (all 4 styles)\n   - Per-story choice: Include pet companion or go solo adventure\n   - Visual consistency: Pet companion rendered consistently throughout story\n   - **Cost**: First child's pet: FREE | Additional children's pets: 4 credits each (~$0.16-$0.40 depending on credit package)\n\n**3. Story Generation Engine (AI-Powered)**\n   - **Text Generation**: Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite API (<$0.001 per story - negligible cost)\n   - **Image Generation**: Google Nano Banana - 6 images per story = **$0.234 per story** (main cost driver)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
