{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '400,800p' docs/PRD.md\"","aggregated_output":"/opt/homebrew/Library/Homebrew/cmd/shellenv.sh: line 18: /bin/ps: Operation not permitted\n   - Clear, professional, trustworthy design\n   - Transparent pricing and no hidden fees\n   - Privacy and safety messaging front-and-center\n   - Quick setup flow (<3 minutes to first story)\n   - Comprehensive but optional controls\n\n**Critical User Flows:**\n\n**Flow 1: First-Time User Onboarding (Conversion-Critical)**\n1. Download app → Welcome screen\n2. \"Create Your Hero\" → Upload child photo (2 photos)\n3. Select 4 art styles → Avatar generated in 30 seconds\n4. \"Meet Your Companion\" → Upload pet photo (optional)\n5. Choose first adventure → Generate first FREE story\n6. Child reads story → \"One more!\" moment\n7. **Paywall appears**: \"Create unlimited stories - Choose your plan\"\n8. Parent subscribes → Unlock full experience\n\n**Time to first story: <5 minutes (critical for trial conversion)**\n\n**Flow 2: Returning User (Engagement Loop)**\n1. Open app → \"Welcome back, [Child Name]!\"\n2. View story library or \"Create New Story\"\n3. Choose adventure type, art style, include pet?\n4. Generate story (30 seconds)\n5. Read/share story\n6. Return to library or create another\n\n**Flow 3: Subscription Management (Parent)**\n1. Access via web dashboard or in-app parent section\n2. View current plan and usage (e.g., \"18 of 30 stories used this month\")\n3. Upgrade/downgrade tier or manage billing\n4. View child's story history and activity\n\n---\n\n## Functional Requirements (Complete)\n\n### FR1: User Management & Authentication\n\n**FR1.1: COPPA-Compliant Parent Account Creation**\n- Parent must create account with verifiable information (email, credit card for age verification)\n- Multi-step verification: Email verification + payment method\n- Accept Terms of Service and Privacy Policy (child-friendly summary provided)\n- Compliance: Meets COPPA verifiable parental consent requirements\n\n**FR1.2: Child Profile Creation & Management**\n- Parent creates child profile(s) within parent account\n- Required fields: Child's first name, birth month/year (for age-appropriate content)\n- Optional fields: Interests, favorite colors, reading level\n- Multiple child profiles per parent account (family plan support)\n- Child profile selection on app launch (no login required for child)\n\n**FR1.3: Authentication & Security**\n- Parent dashboard: Secure login with email/password\n- Optional 2FA for enhanced security\n- Biometric unlock for parent section in mobile app\n- Session management: Auto-logout after inactivity\n- Password reset flow via email\n\n---\n\n### FR2: Avatar & Pet Creation System\n\n**FR2.1: Child Avatar Generation**\n- Upload 2 photos: Portrait (face) + full-body (for poses/actions)\n- AI processing: Generate avatar in 4 art styles (Pixar, 2D, Anime, Watercolor)\n- Generation time: <60 seconds for all 4 styles\n- Preview: Side-by-side comparison of styles\n- Storage: Avatars stored permanently, source photos deleted in 24-48 hours\n- Privacy: Audit log of photo upload and deletion timestamps\n\n**FR2.2: Pet Companion Creation**\n- Upload 1-2 pet photos\n- AI processing: Transform into magical companion in selected art style\n- Pet type detection: Dog, cat, other (affects companion role in stories)\n- Optional: Assign pet name and personality traits\n- Storage: Same privacy protocol as avatar photos\n\n**FR2.3: Avatar & Pet Management**\n- View/edit saved avatars and pets\n- Regenerate in different styles\n- Delete and create new avatar (resets trial if applicable)\n- Associate avatar/pet with specific child profile\n\n---\n\n### FR3: Story Generation Engine\n\n**FR3.1: Story Configuration & Selection**\n- Choose adventure type: Superhero Rescue, Treasure Hunt, Magic Training (MVP templates)\n- Select art style: Must match avatar style chosen\n- Include pet companion: Yes/No toggle\n- Age-appropriate adaptation: Auto-adjust complexity based on child's age\n- Story length: Short (5 min), Medium (10 min) - user preference\n\n**FR3.2: AI Story Generation**\n- Text generation: Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite API\n  - Input: Adventure template, child name, age, pet details, art style\n  - Output: 500-2000 token story narrative\n  - Personalization: Child is protagonist, pet is companion, age-appropriate themes\n- Image generation: Google Nano Banana API\n  - Generate 6 images per story: Avatar, pet, 4 scene illustrations\n  - Consistent art style across all images\n  - Visual quality: 1024x1024 resolution minimum\n- Generation time: <30 seconds total for complete story\n- Error handling: Retry logic, fallback templates if API fails\n\n**FR3.3: Content Safety & Moderation**\n- Pre-generation filtering: Block inappropriate prompts or inputs\n- Post-generation review: AI content moderation on generated text/images\n- Flagging system: Auto-flag potentially inappropriate content for human review\n- Parent reporting: Allow parents to flag stories as inappropriate\n- Blocklist: Maintain list of banned themes, words, image elements\n\n**FR3.4: Story Metadata & Tracking**\n- Each story tagged with: Adventure type, art style, generation date, child profile\n- Reading progress: Track if story started, completed\n- Favorites: Allow child to mark favorite stories\n- Re-read tracking: Count re-reads (popular stories for analytics)\n\n---\n\n### FR4: Credit-Based Monetization System (Primary)\n\n**FR4.1: Credit Wallet & Visibility**\n- Shared family wallet: Parents see current credit balance on dashboard + mobile\n- Action-level costs: Surface costs next to CTA (Avatar: 4 credits, Pet: 4 credits, Story: 10 credits)\n- Free allowances: First child avatar + pet free; 20 generic stories always free\n- Low balance guardrails: Inline warnings at <20 credits, hard block at 0 with purchase CTA\n\n**FR4.2: Credit Purchase Flow**\n- Web checkout via Stripe (20/50/100 credit packs), Apple/Google IAP for mobile\n- Saved payment methods on web for faster repurchase; restore purchases on mobile\n- Receipts stored in transaction history with platform + external IDs\n- Purchase confirmation: Updated balance, receipt email, and in-app toast\n\n**FR4.3: Credit Deduction & Enforcement**\n- Deduct credits atomically per action (avatar, pet, story) with idempotency keys\n- Prevent duplicate charges on retries; show friendly errors when balance insufficient\n- Re-reads never cost credits; generic stories always free\n- Audit trail of credit transactions (type, amount, related story/avatar/pet)\n\n**FR4.4: Credit Promotions & Bonuses**\n- Promo credits: Marketing bonus codes and support-issued credits (type `BONUS`)\n- Starter bonus: 10 bonus credits on first purchase to encourage first top-up\n- Refund/rollbacks: Admin can issue `REFUND` credit transactions tied to purchase ID\n\n**FR4.5: Legacy Subscription Handling (Deprecated)**\n- Legacy subscription tables kept for audit only; no new subscriptions sold\n- If old subscription webhook fires, log and instruct user to move to credits\n- UI surfaces a migration notice for any legacy subscribers directing to credit packs\n\n---\n\n### FR5: Story Library & Content Management\n\n**FR5.1: Personal Story Library**\n- Display all stories generated by child profile\n- Sort options: Most recent, favorites, by adventure type\n- Search/filter: By art style, pet inclusion, date range\n- Grid view with story cover image (first scene)\n- Story metadata: Title (auto-generated), date created, read count\n\n**FR5.2: Story Reading Experience**\n- Full-screen immersive reading mode\n- Page-turn animation between scenes\n- Text-to-speech option (device TTS, post-MVP: voice cloning)\n- Progress tracking: Remember reading position\n- \"Read Again\" vs \"Continue Reading\" logic\n\n**FR5.3: Story Sharing & Export**\n- Share story as PDF (printable storybook)\n- Share via email/messaging to family (not social media - COPPA)\n- Export as image gallery\n- Watermark: \"Created with HeroKid\" on shared content\n\n**FR5.4: Offline Access**\n- Auto-cache last 10 stories per child for offline viewing\n- Manual download: Allow parent to select stories to save offline\n- Sync: Re-sync stories when connection available\n- Storage management: Warn if storage full, allow deletion\n\n---\n\n### FR6: Parental Controls & Monitoring\n\n**FR6.1: Content Monitoring**\n- View all stories generated by each child\n- Reading analytics: Stories per week, favorite adventure types, engagement time\n- Content review: Parent can preview any story before child sees it (optional setting)\n- Inappropriate content flag: Report story to support team\n\n**FR6.2: Privacy & Data Management**\n- COPPA compliance dashboard: View data collected, photo deletion logs\n- Data export: Download all child data (GDPR-K right to portability)\n- Data deletion: Request full account and child data deletion\n- Privacy policy: Accessible in simple, child-friendly language\n- Audit trail: Log of all major actions (account creation, photo uploads/deletions, credit purchases/deductions)\n\n**FR6.3: App Usage Controls**\n- Set daily/weekly story generation limits (parental control of credit spending)\n- Quiet hours: Disable story generation during certain times (e.g., bedtime)\n- Content filters: Block specific adventure types or themes\n- Age progression: Update child age to adjust content complexity\n\n---\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n### Performance\n\n**Response Time:**\n- App launch: <3 seconds on mid-range devices\n- Story generation: <30 seconds total (critical for user experience)\n- Page navigation: <200ms for instant feel\n- Image loading: Progressive rendering, <2 seconds for full quality\n- API timeout: 45 seconds max before fallback/error\n\n**Scalability:**\n- Support 1,000+ concurrent story generation requests (MVP target)\n- Handle 100,000+ registered users with consistent performance\n- Database: Optimized queries for story retrieval (<100ms)\n- CDN: Global content delivery for avatar/story images\n\n**Throughput:**\n- Process 50+ story generations per minute during peak hours\n- Handle 10,000+ API requests per hour (text + image generation)\n\n### Security\n\n**Data Protection:**\n- End-to-end encryption for all user data in transit (TLS 1.3)\n- Encryption at rest for sensitive data (child profiles, payment info)\n- PCI DSS compliance for payment processing (via Stripe)\n- Secure photo upload with signed URLs and time-limited access\n\n**Authentication & Authorization:**\n- Industry-standard password hashing (bcrypt, min 12 rounds)\n- JWT tokens for API authentication with short expiration\n- Role-based access: Parent vs child context separation\n- Rate limiting on authentication endpoints (prevent brute force)\n\n**COPPA Compliance:**\n- Verifiable parental consent before any data collection\n- Minimal data collection: Only what's necessary for service\n- No behavioral tracking or targeted advertising\n- Photo retention: Maximum 24-48 hours, then permanent deletion\n- Third-party data sharing: None (all processing in-house or via compliant APIs)\n- Data deletion: Honor parent requests within 30 days\n\n**Privacy-First Architecture:**\n- No cookies for tracking (only essential session cookies)\n- No third-party analytics SDKs that collect PII\n- No social media integrations (prevent accidental data sharing)\n- Clear, accessible privacy policy in parent and child-friendly versions\n\n### Accessibility\n\n**Must comply with WCAG 2.1 Level AA for parent-facing interfaces:**\n- Color contrast: Minimum 4.5:1 for text\n- Keyboard navigation: Full app navigable without mouse/touch\n- Screen reader support: ARIA labels on all interactive elements\n- Text resizing: UI scales with system font size\n- Focus indicators: Clear visual focus for keyboard users\n\n**Child-Friendly Accessibility:**\n- Large touch targets: Minimum 44×44 points (iOS HIG standard)\n- Simple language: Age-appropriate vocabulary and instructions\n- Audio cues: Optional sound effects for feedback\n- Color-blind friendly: Don't rely solely on color to convey info\n\n### Reliability & Availability\n\n**Uptime:** 99.5% availability (maximum 3.65 hours downtime per month)\n**Backup:** Daily automated backups with 30-day retention\n**Disaster Recovery:** Recovery Time Objective (RTO) <4 hours\n**Error Handling:**\n- Graceful degradation: App usable even if some features fail\n- Retry logic: Auto-retry failed API calls (exponential backoff)\n- User-friendly error messages: Never show technical errors to children\n\n### Integration Requirements\n\n**Google AI APIs:**\n- Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite for text generation\n- Google Nano Banana for image generation\n- API key management: Secure storage, rotation policy\n- Rate limiting: Monitor usage to avoid quota exhaustion\n- Cost monitoring: Alert when API costs exceed thresholds\n\n**Payment Processing:**\n- Apple App Store IAP SDK (iOS) for credit packs\n- Google Play Billing Library (Android) for credit packs\n- Stripe API for web credit purchases\n- Webhook handling for credit purchase events (success, refund, chargeback)\n\n**Platform Infrastructure (Supabase + Vercel):**\n- Supabase Storage: Avatar and story image hosting with lifecycle deletion policies\n- Vercel Serverless Functions: tRPC API routes and background jobs running close to users\n- Supabase PostgreSQL: Relational + JSONB storage for parents, children, credit packs/transactions, and story payloads; legacy subscription tables retained for audit only\n- Supabase Auth: Centralized authentication, parental consent flows, and audit logging hooks\n- Vercel Edge Network & GitHub Actions: Global CDN distribution plus automated CI/CD for previews and production\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Planning & Roadmap\n\n### Phase 1: MVP Development & Beta Launch (Months 1-4)\n\n**Goal:** Build core functionality, validate product-market fit with closed beta\n\n**Key Milestones:**\n- Month 1: Backend API + avatar generation working\n- Month 2: Story generation engine + mobile app (basic UI)\n- Month 3: Credit wallet + purchase flows + COPPA compliance hardening\n- Month 4: Beta launch with 100-500 families\n\n**Success Metrics:**\n- ✅ Free-to-credit conversion: >25% of active families purchase first pack\n- ✅ Repeat purchase rate: 60%+ within 30 days of first pack\n- ✅ Story completion rate: >80%\n- ✅ Parent NPS: >50\n\n**Beta Strategy:**\n- Recruit via parenting forums, social media, personal network\n- Free trial for all beta users (unlimited for testing)\n- Weekly feedback sessions with parents\n- Iterate rapidly based on usage data and feedback\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Public Launch & Growth (Months 5-12)\n\n**Goal:** Scale to 10,000+ users, achieve positive unit economics, refine product\n\n**Launch Strategy:**\n- App Store & Play Store launch (Kids Category)\n- PR campaign: \"AI bedtime stories that comply with new COPPA rules\"\n- Content marketing: Parent blogs, podcasts, YouTube reviews\n- Referral program: Give 1 week free premium for each referral\n\n**Key Features to Add:**\n- Audio narration (Google Text-to-Speech API)\n- More adventure templates (5-7 total)\n- Story remix: Regenerate story in different art style\n- Print/export as PDF storybook\n\n**Growth Targets:**\n- 10,000 total users\n- 2,000-3,000 paid subscribers (20-30% conversion)\n- Monthly recurring revenue (MRR): $20,000-$30,000\n- Path to profitability visible\n\n**Optimization Focus:**\n- A/B test paywall messaging and tier presentation\n- Optimize trial length (2 vs 3 free stories)\n- Test pricing ($7.99 vs $9.99 as default tier)\n- Improve onboarding conversion (photo upload friction)\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Profitability & Expansion (Months 13-24)\n\n**Goal:** Reach breakeven, expand feature set, explore new markets\n\n**Revenue Goals:**\n- 50,000+ total users\n- 10,000-15,000 paid subscribers\n- MRR: $100,000+ (achievable at 10k × $9.99)\n- Profitable or close to breakeven\n\n**Product Expansion:**\n- Family voice cloning (ElevenLabs integration) - Premium feature\n- Multiple pets per story\n- Interactive choice points (choose-your-adventure elements)\n- Educational integration: Reading comprehension questions\n\n**Market Expansion:**\n- Localization: Spanish language stories (large US Hispanic market)\n- B2B pilot: Schools/libraries (site license model)\n- International: UK, Canada, Australia (English-speaking)\n\n**Team Growth:**\n- Hire marketing lead (organic growth + paid acquisition)\n- Hire content moderator (handle story flagging at scale)\n- Contract educators for curriculum tie-ins\n\n---\n\n### Key Risks & Mitigation Strategies\n\n**Risk 1: Trial-to-Paid Conversion <10%**\n- **Impact**: Acquisition costs too high, path to profitability blocked\n- **Mitigation**:\n  - A/B test paywall messaging (\"100% Safe\" vs \"Unlimited Creativity\")\n  - Shorten trial (1-2 stories) to create urgency\n  - Add social proof (testimonials from beta families)\n  - Offer time-limited discount for first month\n\n**Risk 2: Heavy Users Destroy Margins**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
