{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' docs/architecture.md\"","aggregated_output":"/opt/homebrew/Library/Homebrew/cmd/shellenv.sh: line 18: /bin/ps: Operation not permitted\n# HeroKid - Architecture Document\n\n**Author:** Doğan\n**Date:** 2025-11-12\n**Project:** HeroKid - AI-Powered Personalized Storytelling Platform\n**Version:** 1.0\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nHeroKid's architecture is built on a modern **Turborepo monorepo** foundation, enabling seamless code sharing between mobile (Expo React Native) and web (Next.js 15) platforms while maintaining platform-specific optimizations. The architecture prioritizes **type safety, developer velocity, and COPPA compliance** through strategic technology choices.\n\n**Key Architectural Decisions:**\n\n1. **Type-Safe Full-Stack:** tRPC provides end-to-end TypeScript type safety from client to server, eliminating entire classes of runtime errors and reducing API documentation burden.\n\n2. **All-in-One Backend:** Supabase (PostgreSQL) serves as database, authentication, and file storage, accelerating MVP development while maintaining enterprise-grade security and COPPA compliance through Row Level Security and built-in encryption.\n\n3. **Modern React Architecture:** Next.js 15 App Router with React Server Components minimizes client-side state, while Zustand handles necessary global state across mobile and web platforms.\n\n4. **AI Integration Layer:** Dedicated `packages/ai` isolates Gemini (text) and Imagen (images) integrations with retry logic and cost monitoring, protecting margins through tier enforcement.\n\n5. **Privacy-First Design:** Photo deletion audit trails, encrypted storage, and parental authentication without child credentials ensure COPPA compliance is architectural, not bolted-on.\n\n**Performance Strategy:** <30 second story generation through parallel AI API calls, aggressive caching with TanStack Query, and Vercel edge deployment for global low-latency access.\n\n**Scalability Path:** Turborepo's intelligent caching enables fast local development and CI/CD builds. Supabase + Vercel serverless architecture scales automatically from MVP (1K concurrent users) to growth phase (10K+ paid subscribers) without infrastructure rewrites.\n\nThis architecture balances rapid MVP delivery (6-month timeline, <$500K budget) with long-term scalability, positioning HeroKid to reach profitability while maintaining the flexibility to evolve as the product grows.\n\n---\n\n## Project Context Understanding\n\n**Project Type:** Medium-High Complexity Multi-Platform Application\n**Domain:** Educational Technology (EdTech) with AI Integration\n**Platforms:** iOS Mobile App, Android Mobile App, Next.js Web Dashboard\n\n### Core Functionality\nHeroKid is an AI-powered personalized storytelling platform that transforms children aged 5-12 into the heroes of their own adventures alongside their real pets as magical companions.\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Multi-avatar creation system generating 4 professional art styles (Pixar 3D, 2D Cartoon, Anime, Watercolor)\n- Pet companion integration transforming real pets into magical story characters\n- AI story generation engine using Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite (text) + Google Nano Banana (images)\n- Credit-based monetization model (20/50/100 credit packages at $1.99/$3.99/$6.99)\n- Personal story library with offline viewing capability\n- COPPA-compliant parental controls and privacy management\n\n### Critical Non-Functional Requirements\n\n**Privacy & Compliance:**\n- COPPA and GDPR-K compliance mandatory\n- Photo deletion within 24-48 hours after avatar generation\n- End-to-end encryption for all user data\n- No third-party behavioral tracking or advertising\n- Audit trails for compliance demonstration\n\n**Performance:**\n- Story generation: <30 seconds total\n- App launch: <3 seconds on mid-range devices\n- Support 1000+ concurrent users in MVP\n- Page navigation: <200ms for instant feel\n\n**Security:**\n- PCI DSS compliance for payment processing\n- TLS 1.3 for data in transit\n- Encryption at rest for sensitive data\n- Industry-standard password hashing (bcrypt)\n- JWT tokens with short expiration\n\n**Content Safety:**\n- Multi-layered AI content moderation\n- Age-appropriate content filtering (3 age groups: 5-7, 8-10, 11-12)\n- Family-friendly themes exclusively\n- Parent reporting mechanisms\n\n### Technical Scope\n\n**Platform Deliverables:**\n1. iOS mobile app (iOS 14+, iPhone and iPad)\n2. Android mobile app (Android 8+, phones and tablets)\n3. Next.js web dashboard (parental portal and credit management)\n4. Backend API services (microservices architecture)\n5. Payment processing integration (Stripe + Apple/Google IAP for credit purchases)\n\n**Major Feature Areas:**\n- FR1: User Management & Authentication (COPPA-compliant)\n- FR2: Avatar & Pet Creation System (AI image generation, 4 credits per additional child)\n- FR3: Story Generation Engine (AI text + image generation, 10 credits per customized story)\n- FR4: Credit-Based Monetization System (flexible per-use spending, no subscriptions)\n- FR5: Story Library & Content Management (offline capability, 20+ free generic stories)\n- FR6: Parental Controls & Monitoring (credit management + privacy dashboard)\n\n### Scale & Constraints\n\n**MVP Targets:**\n- 10,000+ registered users\n- 1,000+ concurrent story generation requests\n- <$500K development cost\n- 6-month timeline to launch\n\n**Growth Phase:**\n- 50,000+ total users\n- 15,000-20,000 active credit purchasers\n- $100K+ monthly recurring revenue (MRR)\n\n**Key Challenges:**\n- Real-time AI generation with strict performance constraints\n- Privacy-first architecture with photo deletion audit trails\n- Age-adaptive content complexity across 3 developmental stages\n- Cross-platform visual consistency for personalized avatars\n- Cost management for AI API usage (margins depend on credit model pricing and deduction logic)\n\n---\n\n## Project Initialization\n\n**First Implementation Story: Initialize Monorepo Structure**\n\nThe project should be initialized using Turborepo with the following commands:\n\n```bash\n# Step 1: Initialize Turborepo monorepo\nnpx create-turbo@latest\n\n# Step 2: Add Expo mobile app\ncd apps\nnpx create-expo-app@latest mobile\n\n# Step 3: Add Next.js web dashboard\nnpx create-next-app@latest web --typescript --tailwind --app --turbopack\n\n# Step 4: Set up shared packages structure\nmkdir -p packages/ui packages/api packages/database packages/config\n```\n\n**What the Starter Provides:**\n\n- **Turborepo**: Monorepo orchestration with intelligent caching\n- **TypeScript**: Full type safety across all packages (default in Next.js 15 and Expo)\n- **Build tooling**: Turborepo task runner for coordinated builds\n- **Package management**: Workspace configuration for shared dependencies\n- **Project structure**: Apps and packages separation\n\n---\n\n## Decision Summary\n\n| Category | Decision | Version | Affects Epics | Rationale |\n| -------- | -------- | ------- | ------------- | --------- |\n| Monorepo Tool | Turborepo | Latest | All epics | Enables code sharing between mobile and web, intelligent caching for fast builds, scalable architecture for microservices |\n| Mobile Framework | Expo (React Native) | SDK 54+ | FR1, FR2, FR3, FR5, FR6 | Cross-platform iOS/Android from single codebase, managed workflow reduces native complexity, OTA updates capability |\n| Web Framework | Next.js | 15.1.8+ | FR1, FR4, FR6 | App Router for modern React patterns, built-in API routes, SSR/SSG for performance, Vercel deployment optimized |\n| Language | TypeScript | 5.0+ | All epics | Type safety prevents runtime errors, better IDE support, shared types across platforms |\n| Build Tool (Web) | Turbopack | Built-in Next.js 15 | Web dashboard | Faster development builds than Webpack, native Next.js integration |\n| API Layer | tRPC | 11.0+ | All epics | End-to-end type safety between client and server, perfect for monorepo setup, eliminates API documentation burden, compile-time error catching |\n| Database & Backend | Supabase (PostgreSQL) | Latest | All epics | All-in-one solution: PostgreSQL database, authentication, file storage, real-time subscriptions, Row Level Security for multi-tenant isolation, built-in COPPA-compliant encryption |\n| ORM | Prisma | 5.0+ | All epics with DB access | Type-safe database client, automatic TypeScript types from schema, excellent with PostgreSQL and Supabase, migration management |\n| Authentication | Supabase Auth | Built-in | FR1, FR4, FR6 | COPPA-compliant approach: parents authenticate, children are profiles without credentials, biometric unlock support, 2FA optional |\n| Payment Processing (Web) | Stripe | Latest | FR4 | Credit card processing for credit purchases, avoids 30% app store fee, PCI DSS compliant |\n| Payment Processing (iOS) | Apple In-App Purchase (StoreKit 2) | Latest | FR4 | Required for credit purchases on iOS, 30% fee, handles transaction processing |\n| Payment Processing (Android) | Google Play Billing | Latest | FR4 | Required for credit purchases on Android, 30% fee, handles transaction processing |\n| State Management (Mobile) | Zustand | 4.0+ | Mobile app | Lightweight, minimal boilerplate, TypeScript-friendly, shared state across components |\n| State Management (Web) | React Server Components + Zustand | Built-in Next.js + 4.0+ | Web dashboard | Minimize client state with RSC, Zustand for necessary client state |\n| Server State/Caching | TanStack Query (React Query) | 5.0+ | All client apps | Automatic caching, background refetching, perfect tRPC integration, optimistic updates |\n| UI Components (Mobile) | NativeWind + Expo UI | Latest | Mobile app | Tailwind CSS for React Native, consistent styling with web, native feel |\n| UI Components (Web) | Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui | Latest | Web dashboard | Beautiful accessible components, pre-styled with Tailwind, customizable |\n| File Storage & CDN | Supabase Storage | Built-in | FR2, FR3, FR5 | Avatar and story image storage, automatic CDN distribution, signed URLs for privacy, photo deletion audit trail for COPPA compliance |\n| AI Text Generation | Google Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite | Latest | FR3 | Cost-effective story generation (<$0.001 per story), fast response times, age-appropriate content capabilities |\n| AI Image Generation | Google Nano Banana (Imagen 3) | Latest | FR2, FR3 | Multi-style avatar generation, consistent character rendering, $0.039 per image, supports Pixar/2D/Anime/Watercolor styles |\n| Deployment (Web) | Vercel | Latest | Web dashboard | Optimized for Next.js, automatic HTTPS, preview deployments, edge network |\n| Deployment (API) | Vercel Serverless Functions | Built-in | tRPC API | Automatic scaling, pay-per-use, integrates with Next.js API routes |\n| Deployment (Mobile) | Expo Application Services (EAS) | Latest | Mobile apps | OTA updates, managed builds, TestFlight/Play Store distribution |\n| Error Tracking | Sentry | Latest | All platforms | Production error monitoring, performance tracking, privacy-compliant, works across mobile/web/API |\n| Analytics | PostHog | Latest | All platforms | Privacy-first analytics, feature flags, A/B testing, GDPR/COPPA compliant, self-hostable |\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Cutting Concerns\n\nThese patterns apply to ALL epics and stories. Every AI agent MUST follow these conventions.\n\n### Error Handling\n\n**Standard Error/Success Response Format:**\n```typescript\ntype ErrorResponse = {\n  success: false;\n  error: {\n    code: string;        // e.g., \"PAYMENT_FAILED\", \"AI_GENERATION_ERROR\"\n    message: string;     // User-friendly message\n    details?: unknown;   // Technical details (dev only)\n  }\n}\n\ntype SuccessResponse<T> = {\n  success: true;\n  data: T;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
