{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' docs/epics.md\"","aggregated_output":"/opt/homebrew/Library/Homebrew/cmd/shellenv.sh: line 18: /bin/ps: Operation not permitted\n# HeroKid - Epic Breakdown\n\n**Author:** Doğan\n**Date:** 2025-11-12\n**Project Level:** Medium-High Complexity\n**Target Scale:** MVP: 1,000+ concurrent users → Scale: 100,000+ registered users\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document provides the complete epic and story breakdown for HeroKid, decomposing the requirements from the [PRD](./PRD.md) into implementable stories.\n\n### Epic Structure\n\nHeroKid's MVP implementation is organized into **6 epics** following a bottom-up dependency order:\n\n1. **Foundation & Infrastructure** - Technical foundation enabling all subsequent development\n2. **COPPA-Compliant User Management** - Parent accounts and child profiles with regulatory compliance\n3. **Multi-Avatar & Pet Creation System** - Photo transformation into professional cartoon avatars across 4 art styles\n4. **AI Story Generation Engine** - Personalized, age-appropriate story creation with child's avatar and pet\n5. **Story Library & Reading Experience** - Immersive reading interface and persistent story collection\n6. **Credit Monetization System** - Credit-based wallet and purchases (legacy subscription flow deprecated)\n\n**Sequencing Rationale:** Each epic builds on the previous, with no forward dependencies. Foundation enables accounts, accounts enable avatars, avatars enable stories, stories enable library, and the complete experience enables monetization.\n\n---\n\n## Epic 1: Foundation & Infrastructure\n\n**Goal:** Establish a Supabase + Vercel native foundation that accelerates multi-surface development, enforces COPPA constraints, and keeps deployment friction near-zero.\n\n### Story 1.1: Initialize Turborepo Monorepo with Expo and Next.js\n\nAs a **developer**,\nI want **a Turborepo with Expo (apps/mobile) and Next.js 15 (apps/web) plus shared packages**,\nSo that **mobile, web, and shared logic evolve in lockstep with consistent tooling**.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- Turborepo configured with `apps/mobile`, `apps/web`, and `packages/shared`\n- Expo-managed workflow bootstrapped in `apps/mobile` with EAS configuration files\n- Next.js 15 project initialized in `apps/web` with app router enabled\n- Shared TypeScript config, ESLint, Prettier, and testing tooling live in `packages/shared`\n- Root scripts (`dev`, `build`, `lint`, `test`) orchestrate work across workspaces\n- Documentation in `README` describing workspace layout and commands\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- Use pnpm or npm workspaces (document choice)\n- Configure absolute imports via `tsconfig.base.json`\n\n### Story 1.2: Set Up Supabase Project\n\nAs a **platform engineer**,\nI want **Supabase projects for development and production with Auth, Storage, and PostgreSQL ready**,\nSo that **the product can leverage managed BaaS features without bespoke self-managed infrastructure**.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- `herokid-dev` and `herokid-production` Supabase projects created with linked GitHub repo\n- PostgreSQL databases provisioned with baseline schemas for parents, children, credit packs/transactions (plus legacy subscription tables for audit), audit logs, and photo deletion queues\n- Supabase Auth configured with parental consent policy, child profile restrictions, and email templates\n- Supabase Storage buckets for avatars, story images, and temporary uploads with lifecycle rules (temp bucket auto-deletes within 48h)\n- Row Level Security enabled on all tables with policies for parent vs child access\n- Environment variables documented for local development and Vercel deployments\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- Capture schema migrations via Prisma or Supabase migration scripts committed to repo\n\n### Story 1.3: Implement tRPC API with Prisma ORM\n\nAs a **developer**,\nI want **type-safe tRPC routers backed by Prisma models**,\nSo that **mobile and web clients get shared types without duplicating API contracts**.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- Prisma installed and configured inside `packages/shared` (or dedicated `packages/db`) with Supabase connection strings per environment\n- Prisma schema includes parents, child_profiles, credit_packs, credit_transactions, audit_logs, stories, photo_deletion_jobs tables aligned with architecture doc; legacy subscription tables marked deprecated\n- `apps/web/src/server/trpc` hosts base router, context (auth, db), and at least one sample procedure (e.g., health/status)\n- tRPC client utilities exported for both `apps/web` and `apps/mobile`\n- Code generation or inferred types verified via sample query/mutation in each app\n- Unit tests cover router context initialization and Prisma client instantiation\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- Enforce strict type safety with `@trpc/server@next` and `@trpc/client`\n\n### Story 1.4: Configure Vercel Deployment\n\nAs a **DevOps-focused developer**,\nI want **Vercel deployments wired to the repo**,\nSo that **each PR gets previews and main merges auto-deploy to production**.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- GitHub repo connected to Vercel project(s) for `apps/web`\n- Build outputs configured with Turborepo caching (via `turbo.json` + Vercel integration)\n- Environment variables (Supabase anon/service keys, Gemini API key, Stripe keys) configured for Preview and Production environments\n- Preview deployments trigger on every PR, with comments posted back to GitHub\n- Production deployment requires main-branch merge and uses protected env vars\n- Deployment runbook added to `/docs/technical/cicd.md`\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- Use Vercel secrets for Supabase service roles; never expose service role to client bundles\n\n### Story 1.5: Configure EAS (Expo Application Services) for Mobile\n\nAs a **mobile engineer**,\nI want **EAS Build and EAS Update configured**,\nSo that **we can produce signed binaries and ship OTA updates quickly**.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- `eas.json` includes build profiles for development, staging, and production (iOS + Android)\n- Credentials (Apple certificates/profiles, Android keystore) stored in EAS secrets with documented retrieval steps\n- EAS Update channels defined for staging and production; OTA workflow tested end-to-end\n- Expo Application Services linked to repository CI so tagged releases trigger builds\n- Documentation captures how to run `eas build` and `eas update` locally and via CI\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- Enable Expo Router + new architecture where feasible for performance\n\n### Story 1.6: Establish CI/CD Pipeline on GitHub Actions\n\nAs a **team**,\nI want **automated workflows for linting, testing, and deployments**,\nSo that **quality gates and deployments stay consistent**.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs lint, type-check, and tests for all packages with Turborepo caching\n- `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` (or jobs within CI) trigger Vercel deployments and, when tagged, EAS builds\n- Secrets managed via GitHub Environments referencing Supabase/Vercel/EAS tokens\n- Status checks required before merge via branch protection\n- Workflow documentation added to `/docs/technical/cicd.md`\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- Use `actions/cache` with Turborepo remote caching (if available) for faster builds\n\n### Story 1.7: Photo Deletion Audit Trail System\n\nAs a **compliance engineer**,\nI want **automated lifecycle enforcement for sensitive uploads**,\nSo that **HeroKid meets COPPA requirements for photo retention and traceability**.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- Supabase Storage temp bucket enforces lifecycle policy (24-48 hour deletion)\n- PostgreSQL table `photo_deletion_audit` records upload_id, child_profile_id, uploaded_at, deletion_due_at, deletion_performed_at, performed_by\n- Scheduled job (Supabase cron or Vercel Cron) polls for expired uploads, deletes them, and logs completion\n- Admin dashboard (even minimal) or Supabase SQL view exposes deletion status for compliance review\n- Alerts/logging exist for failures so operations can intervene\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- Consider Supabase Edge Functions for cron runner when Vercel Cron not available\n\n### Story 1.8: Health Checks and Monitoring\n\nAs a **maintainer**,\nI want **observable infrastructure**,\nSo that **issues are detected early with clear remediation paths**.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- `/api/health` tRPC procedure (or REST endpoint) returns Supabase connectivity, Prisma status, and build metadata\n- Vercel Analytics enabled for production project with alerts on error spikes\n- Error tracking (Sentry, LogRocket, or similar) instrumented in both apps with environment tagging\n- Lightweight status dashboard (Notion, Supabase dashboard, or custom page) surfaces deployment status, cron job health, and Supabase metrics\n- Runbooks for incident response stored in `/docs/technical/operations.md`\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- Wire Supabase log drains to monitoring provider for consolidated alerts\n## Epic 2: COPPA-Compliant User Management\n\n**Goal:** Enable parents to securely create accounts and manage child profiles while maintaining strict COPPA and GDPR-K compliance through verifiable consent, audit trails, and privacy-first architecture.\n\n### Story 2.1: Parent Account Registration API\n\nAs a **parent**,\nI want **to create an account using my email and password**,\nSo that **I can access HeroKid and manage my children's profiles securely**.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n\n**Given** the tRPC procedure `auth.register` (Next.js API route) exists\n**When** a parent submits registration data: `{email, password, confirmPassword}`\n**Then** the system validates:\n- Email format is valid\n- Password meets security requirements (min 12 characters, mix of uppercase/lowercase/numbers/symbols)\n- Password and confirmPassword match\n- Email is not already registered (Supabase Auth + parents table check)\n\n**And** if validation passes:\n- Calls Supabase Auth `signUp` to create the canonical user (Supabase handles hashing & storage)\n- Parent record is created in `parents` table with `status: 'pending_verification'`, `supabase_user_id`\n- Audit log entry is created: `{action: 'account_created', timestamp, parent_id}`\n- Supabase Auth sends verification email using customized COPPA-compliant template\n\n**And** API returns 201 Created with: `{message: 'Account created, please verify email', parent_id}`\n\n**And** if validation fails, returns structured error response (tRPC error or validation error map)\n\n**Prerequisites:** Story 1.2 (Supabase project configured), Story 1.3 (tRPC + Prisma foundation)\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- Use Supabase service role key on server to perform admin checks while keeping client SDK limited\n- Generate UUID for parent_id (separate from Supabase Auth user id) for relational joins\n- Rate limit: 5 registration attempts per IP per hour (prevent abuse)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
