{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' PROJECT_STATUS_REPORT.md\"","aggregated_output":"/opt/homebrew/Library/Homebrew/cmd/shellenv.sh: line 18: /bin/ps: Operation not permitted\n# HeroKid - Project Status Report\n\n**Date:** December 5, 2025\n**Status:** 🟢 Production Ready (96% Complete)\n**Version:** MVP Candidate\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project Overview\n\nHeroKid is a multi-platform (Web & Mobile) AI-powered storytelling application that transforms children into the heroes of their own adventures. The project uses a monorepo structure managed by Turborepo, sharing core business logic between a Next.js web dashboard and an Expo React Native mobile app.\n\n**Key Value Proposition:**\n- **Personalized Avatars:** Converts child photos into cartoons (Pixar, Anime, etc.) using Google Imagen 3 (Nano Banana).\n- **AI Storytelling:** Generates age-appropriate stories using Google Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite.\n- **Safety First:** Built-in COPPA compliance with automated photo deletion and parental consent flows.\n- **Flexible Monetization:** Pivoted from subscriptions to a high-margin credit-based system ($0.99/story).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture Analysis\n\nThe implementation closely adheres to the architectural vision outlined in `docs/architecture.md`.\n\n| Component | Planned Tech | Actual Implementation | Status |\n|-----------|--------------|-----------------------|--------|\n| **Monorepo** | Turborepo | Turborepo 2.x | ✅ Matches |\n| **Mobile** | Expo (React Native) | Expo SDK 51 + EAS | ✅ Matches |\n| **Web** | Next.js 15 | Next.js 15 App Router | ✅ Matches |\n| **API** | tRPC + Prisma | tRPC v11 + Prisma 5 | ✅ Matches |\n| **Database** | Supabase (PostgreSQL) | Supabase (PostgreSQL 15) | ✅ Matches |\n| **Auth** | Supabase Auth | Supabase Auth (Password/Social) | ✅ Matches |\n| **AI (Text)** | Gemini 1.5/2.0 | Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite | ✅ Upgraded |\n| **AI (Image)** | Imagen 2 | Imagen 3 (Nano Banana) | ✅ Upgraded |\n| **Payment** | Stripe/IAP | Stripe + Apple IAP + Google Play | ✅ Matches |\n\n**Architectural Highlights:**\n- **Type Safety:** End-to-end type safety is achieved via tRPC sharing types between `packages/api` and client apps.\n- **Compliance Infrastructure:** Dedicated audit logging (`AuditLog`, `PhotoDeletionAudit`) is baked into the core data model, not an afterthought.\n- **Hybrid Monetization:** The database schema supports both legacy subscriptions and the new credit-based model (`CreditPack`), allowing for future flexibility.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Feature Implementation Status\n\nBased on `docs/epics.md` and codebase verification:\n\n| Epic | Status | Notes |\n|------|--------|-------|\n| **1. Foundation** | ✅ Complete | CI/CD, Supabase, Vercel, EAS pipelines active. |\n| **2. User Management** | ✅ Complete | COPPA consent flow, Parent/Child profiles, Privacy dashboard. |\n| **3. Avatar Creation** | ✅ Complete | Multi-style generation (Pixar, 2D, Anime, Watercolor), Pet companions. |\n| **4. Story Engine** | ✅ Complete | Age-adaptive prompts, Scene generation, Safety filtering. |\n| **5. Library & Reading** | ✅ Complete | Offline caching, Interactive reading mode, PDF export. |\n| **6. Monetization** | ⚠️ Modified | **Pivot:** Implemented Credit System (1/5/10 packs) instead of Subscriptions. |\n\n**Detailed Findings:**\n- **Credit System:** Fully implemented in `creditsRouter`. Supports cross-platform purchasing (Stripe for Web, IAP for Mobile).\n- **Photo Upload:** Secure signed URL flow with strict 48-hour lifecycle policies for COPPA compliance.\n- **AI Clients:** `NanoBananaClient` implements robust retry logic and concurrent batch generation (8 images < 60s).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Code Quality & Coverage\n\nThe codebase exhibits high professional standards.\n\n- **Organization:** Clear separation of concerns.\n  - `packages/api`: Business logic & tRPC routers.\n  - `packages/database`: Prisma schema & migrations.\n  - `packages/ai`: Isolated AI clients (Gemini/Imagen) with error handling.\n- **Testing:**\n  - **Unit Tests:** High coverage in `packages/api` (e.g., `auth.test.ts`, `credits.test.ts`).\n  - **Integration Tests:** Present for critical flows (`storage-lifecycle.test.mjs`).\n  - **E2E Tests:** Mobile app E2E test suite exists.\n- **Technical Debt:**\n  - **Legacy Code:** `Subscription` models still exist in Prisma schema alongside `CreditPack`. This is safe but should be cleaned up post-launch if the pivot is permanent.\n  - **IAP Verification:** The `verifyApplePurchase` and `verifyGooglePurchase` procedures contain warnings about incomplete receipt verification logic (needs production secrets/setup).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Database & Infrastructure\n\n**Database (Supabase/PostgreSQL):**\n- **Schema:** 27 Models. Well-structured with proper indexes and foreign keys.\n- **Key Models:**\n  - `Parent` & `ChildProfile`: Core user data.\n  - `Story` & `StoryImage`: Content data (JSONB storage for flexible story structures).\n  - `CreditTransaction`: Double-entry ledger for credit history.\n  - `PhotoUpload`: Tracks temporary files for deletion.\n\n**Infrastructure:**\n- **Storage:** Supabase Storage buckets (`avatars`, `story-images`, `temp-uploads`) configured with lifecycle rules.\n- **Compute:** Vercel Serverless Functions (Web/API) + Expo EAS (Mobile).\n\n---\n\n## 6. API Endpoints\n\nThe backend is exposed via tRPC, organized into modular routers:\n\n- `auth`: Registration, Login, COPPA Consent.\n- `credits`: Purchase (Stripe/IAP), Balance check, Deduction logic.\n- `story`: Generation, Retrieval, Progress tracking.\n- `avatar`: Image generation, Style selection.\n- `childProfile`: Management of child profiles.\n- `photoDeletion`: Audit and enforcement APIs.\n\n**Status:** All key routers are implemented and exported in `root.ts`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Frontend Progress\n\n**Web Dashboard (`apps/web`):**\n- **Tech:** Next.js 15 App Router, Tailwind CSS.\n- **Features:** Auth flows, Parent Dashboard, Credit Purchase (`/purchase`), Child Management.\n- **Status:** Complete and integrated with Stripe.\n\n**Mobile App (`apps/mobile`):**\n- **Tech:** Expo (React Native), NativeWind.\n- **Features:** Story Library, Immersive Reading Mode, Avatar Creator.\n- **Status:** Complete, EAS build profiles ready.\n\n---\n\n## 8. AI Integrations\n\n**Text Generation (Gemini):**\n- **Client:** `packages/ai/src/gemini/client.ts`\n- **Model:** `gemini-2.5-flash-lite`\n- **Features:** Age-adaptive prompts (5-7, 8-10, 11-12), Safety settings (Block Medium+).\n\n**Image Generation (Nano Banana):**\n- **Client:** `packages/ai/src/imagen/client.ts`\n- **Model:** Imagen 3 (via Vertex AI)\n- **Features:**\n  - **Parallel Generation:** Uses `Promise.all` to generate 8 avatar variations at once.\n  - **Style Transfer:** Supports 'pixar', '2d', 'anime', 'watercolor'.\n  - **Safety:** Explicit safety score extraction and mapping.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Privacy & Compliance\n\n**COPPA & GDPR-K:**\n- **Consent:** `ParentConsentEvent` tracks IP and timestamp of consent.\n- **Data Minimization:** `PhotoUpload` table tracks temporary files.\n- **Automated Deletion:** `scripts/delete-expired-photos.mjs` runs via Cron to enforce 48-hour deletion of source photos.\n- **Audit:** Immutable `AuditLog` table records all sensitive actions (login, purchase, deletion).\n\n---\n\n## 10. Next Steps & Recommendations\n\n1.  **Security Hardening (Critical):**\n    - Finalize server-side receipt verification for Apple/Google IAP in `creditsRouter`.\n    - Rotate production keys for Supabase and Stripe before public launch.\n\n2.  **Cleanup (Post-Launch):**\n    - Decide on the final monetization model. If strictly credits, remove `Subscription` models from Prisma schema to reduce noise.\n\n3.  **Monitoring:**\n    - Set up alerts for `PhotoDeletionJob` failures to ensure COPPA compliance is never breached.\n    - Monitor AI API costs closely using the built-in tracking in `NanoBananaClient`.\n\n4.  **Launch:**\n    - The project is technically ready for MVP launch (`pnpm build` passes, tests pass).\n    - Proceed with App Store / Play Store submission processes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
