{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_197","type":"reasoning","text":"**Summarizing final report and key findings**\n\nPlaced the executive summary and detailed report in project files for reference. Key findings include: story generation pipeline failures due to environment import bugs (`packages/api/lib/generateStoryAsync.ts`); TRPC authentication cookie mismatches (`apps/web/app/providers.tsx` and `packages/api/src/context.ts`); unauthenticated PDF export route and incorrect imports (`apps/web/app/api/generate-pdf/route.tsx`); credit pack misalignment and incomplete in-app purchase verification (`packages/api/src/routers/credits.ts`); and inconsistent Supabase environment variable naming causing TypeScript errors (`packages/ai/src/storage/sceneImageStorage.ts`). Note that tests have not been run. Suggested next steps: run full test suite to validate fixes, standardize environment variable naming across packages, and implement comprehensive authentication checks on API routes."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_198","type":"agent_message","text":"Updated the requested reports: summary in `.claude/skills/orchestration-skill/logs/results/17aea796.summary.md` and detailed analysis in `.claude/skills/orchestration-skill/logs/results/17aea796_report.md`.\n\nKey findings:\n- Story generation is currently blocked: `packages/api/src/lib/generateStoryAsync.ts` imports a non-existent `env` export and even falls back to the anon Supabase key, so the async worker will fail before hitting Gemini/Imagen.\n- Web auth/tRPC are miswired: the client in `apps/web/app/providers.tsx` never sends Supabase tokens and `packages/api/src/context.ts` only reads Authorization headers, so protected queries (credits/library/etc.) won’t work from the web dashboard.\n- PDF export route is insecure/broken: `apps/web/app/api/generate-pdf/route.tsx` is unauthenticated, uses a service key, and imports `db` that isn’t exported—opens a data leak and fails at runtime.\n- Monetization diverges from the PRD: credit packs are 1/5/10 with incomplete Apple/Google receipt verification (`packages/api/src/routers/credits.ts`); PRD expects 20/50/100 and production-grade verification/webhooks.\n- Supabase key naming is inconsistent (SERVICE_KEY vs SERVICE_ROLE_KEY) across storage/AI/API modules (e.g., `packages/ai/src/storage/sceneImageStorage.ts`), increasing misconfig risk; TypeScript error report indicates unresolved compiler issues.\n\nTests were not run in this pass.\n\nNext steps:\n1) Fix story worker env handling and key usage, then add alerts on job failures.\n2) Align web auth by either reading Supabase cookies in `createContext` or injecting Authorization headers in the web client, and replace dashboard placeholders with real queries.\n3) Secure PDF export and harden payments (align pack sizes to PRD, finish receipt/webhook verification) before further launch steps."}}
